    <dashboard name='Netflix content analysis' type='storyboard'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://public.tableau.com/workbooks/Netflixcontentanalysis_17489707360360/117518652?rev=' id='Netflixcontentanalysis' path='/workbooks/Netflixcontentanalysis_17489707360360' revision='' />
      <style />
      <size sizing-mode='automatic' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98130' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99064' x='468' y='935'>
            <zone h='3855' id='3' type-v2='title' w='99064' x='468' y='935' />
            <zone h='11799' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='99064' x='468' y='4790' />
            <zone h='82476' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='99064' x='468' y='16589'>
              <flipboard active-id='9' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='This dashboard reveals that Netflix&apos;s library is dominated by movies (69.6%), with a significant surge in content additions between 2016 and 2019, peaking in 2018. Despite a slight drop post-2020, Netflix maintains a robust catalog of over 8,800 titles, reflecting its continued focus on diverse content offerings.' captured-sheet='Distribution of TV Shows and Movies in Netflix' id='1'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='How many movies and TV shows are available on Netflix in Bar graph'>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi].[Action (Type)]'>
                          <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[type]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                      <worksheet name='Release year vs count of shows'>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi].[Action (Type)]'>
                          <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[type]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='This dashboard highlights a sharp rise in Netflix content additions between 2015 and 2019, peaking in 2019 with over 1,400 titles, followed by a decline in 2020 and 2021 likely due to production challenges. Monthly trends show consistent content uploads, while the release year analysis indicates a rapid expansion in Netflix’s catalog from 2010 onward, reflecting the platform’s streaming boom.' captured-sheet='Trend in addind contents in Netflix by year' id='2'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='How many movies and TV shows are available on Netflix in Bar graph'>
                        <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi'>
                          <column-instance column='[date_added]' derivation='Month' name='[mn:date_added:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
                        </datasource-dependencies>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi].[Action (MONTH(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[mn:date_added:ok]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi].[Action (YEAR(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[yr:date_added:ok]' user:ui-action-filter='[Action4_74A54192369C48CDBD0C15D117EDE213]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                      <worksheet name='Release year vs count of shows'>
                        <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi'>
                          <column-instance column='[date_added]' derivation='Month' name='[mn:date_added:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
                        </datasource-dependencies>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi].[Action (MONTH(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[mn:date_added:ok]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi].[Action (YEAR(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[yr:date_added:ok]' user:ui-action-filter='[Action4_74A54192369C48CDBD0C15D117EDE213]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                      <worksheet name='Titles added to Netflix each Month'>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[Action (YEAR(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[yr:date_added:ok]' user:ui-action-filter='[Action4_74A54192369C48CDBD0C15D117EDE213]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                      <worksheet name='Trend in titles added to Netflix each year'>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[Action (MONTH(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[mn:date_added:ok]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[mn:date_added:ok]'>
                          <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[mn:date_added:ok]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-exclude='true' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                        <selection-collection />
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='This dashboard shows that the United States leads Netflix content production, followed by the UK and France, with the highest multi-country collaborations. Genre-wise, dramas, documentaries, and comedies are the most common across top countries, while India and Japan contribute significantly with regional favorites like international TV shows and anime.' captured-sheet='Country-wise content count' id='3'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Number of contents with respect to countries'>
                        <style delta-type='added'>
                          <style-rule element='axis'>
                            <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.12m87it0vovc3b17tl81r1q3x001].[Latitude (generated)]' field-type='quantitative' max='12718585.506073151' min='-8520234.090090245' projection='EPSG:3857' range-type='fixed' scope='rows' type='space' />
                            <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.12m87it0vovc3b17tl81r1q3x001].[Longitude (generated)]' field-type='quantitative' max='27826881.952913616' min='-14880365.879756533' projection='EPSG:3857' range-type='fixed' scope='cols' type='space' />
                          </style-rule>
                        </style>
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='This dashboard shows that TV-MA (36%) and TV-14 (25%) are the most common Netflix ratings, indicating a strong focus on mature and teen audiences, with dramas and comedies leading across all rating segments.' captured-sheet='Ratings by content type' id='4' />
                  <story-point caption='One-third of Netflix titles are added with no delay, while others show an average delay of about 2 years, peaking around 2019 before improving.' captured-sheet='Delay rate throughout years' id='5'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Average delay in adding'>
                        <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a'>
                          <column-instance column='[date_added]' derivation='Year' name='[yr:date_added:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
                        </datasource-dependencies>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[Action (YEAR(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='member' level='[yr:date_added:ok]' member='2019' user:ui-domain='database' user:ui-enumeration='inclusive' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                      <worksheet name='Delay rate throughout the year'>
                        <selection-collection>
                          <tuple-selection>
                            <tuple-reference>
                              <tuple-descriptor>
                                <pane-descriptor>
                                  <x-fields>
                                    <field>[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[yr:date_added:ok]</field>
                                  </x-fields>
                                  <y-fields>
                                    <field>[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[cnt:show_id:qk]</field>
                                  </y-fields>
                                </pane-descriptor>
                                <columns>
                                  <field>[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[cnt:show_id:qk]</field>
                                  <field>[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[yr:date_added:ok]</field>
                                </columns>
                              </tuple-descriptor>
                              <tuple>
                                <value>1345</value>
                                <value>2019</value>
                              </tuple>
                            </tuple-reference>
                          </tuple-selection>
                        </selection-collection>
                      </worksheet>
                      <worksheet name='Delay ratio'>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[Action (YEAR(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='member' level='[yr:date_added:ok]' member='2019' user:ui-domain='database' user:ui-enumeration='inclusive' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                      <worksheet name='How many movies and TV shows are available on Netflix'>
                        <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi'>
                          <column-instance column='[date_added]' derivation='Year' name='[yr:date_added:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
                        </datasource-dependencies>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi].[Action (YEAR(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='member' level='[yr:date_added:ok]' member='2019' user:ui-domain='database' user:ui-enumeration='inclusive' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                      <worksheet name='Release year vs count of shows'>
                        <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi'>
                          <column-instance column='[date_added]' derivation='Year' name='[yr:date_added:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
                        </datasource-dependencies>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi].[Action (YEAR(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='member' level='[yr:date_added:ok]' member='2019' user:ui-domain='database' user:ui-enumeration='inclusive' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='Average movie duration on Netflix is about 100 minutes, with most movies clustered between 90–110 minutes. For TV shows, 1-season titles dominate, suggesting Netflix frequently offers limited series or short-format content.' captured-sheet='Average duration for movies and TV Shows' id='6' />
                  <story-point caption='This dashboard shows that Dramas, Comedies, and Action &amp; Adventure have consistently been the most popular genres on Netflix over time. Additionally, Netflix adds 700–800 new titles monthly, with Dramas leading in total genre distribution.' captured-sheet='Genre trend throughout the year' id='7'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Count of sub-genres'>
                        <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi'>
                          <column-instance column='[date_added]' derivation='Year' name='[yr:date_added:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
                        </datasource-dependencies>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi].[Action (YEAR(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='member' level='[yr:date_added:ok]' member='2018' user:ui-domain='database' user:ui-enumeration='inclusive' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                      <worksheet name='Distribution of contents by genres'>
                        <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi'>
                          <column-instance column='[date_added]' derivation='Year' name='[yr:date_added:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
                        </datasource-dependencies>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi].[Action (YEAR(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='member' level='[yr:date_added:ok]' member='2018' user:ui-domain='database' user:ui-enumeration='inclusive' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                      <worksheet name='How many movies and TV shows are available on Netflix in Bar graph'>
                        <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi'>
                          <column-instance column='[date_added]' derivation='Year' name='[yr:date_added:ok]' pivot='key' type='ordinal' />
                        </datasource-dependencies>
                        <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.14prv9d1gczplo14pzulh05a14xi].[Action (YEAR(Date Added))]'>
                          <groupfilter function='member' level='[yr:date_added:ok]' member='2018' user:ui-domain='database' user:ui-enumeration='inclusive' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
                        </filter>
                      </worksheet>
                      <worksheet name='Trend in titles added to Netflix each year'>
                        <selection-collection>
                          <tuple-selection>
                            <tuple-reference>
                              <tuple-descriptor>
                                <pane-descriptor>
                                  <x-fields>
                                    <field>[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[yr:date_added:ok]</field>
                                  </x-fields>
                                  <y-fields>
                                    <field>[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[cnt:show_id:qk]</field>
                                  </y-fields>
                                </pane-descriptor>
                                <columns>
                                  <field>[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[cnt:show_id:qk]</field>
                                  <field>[federated.0qtherb0uk6bov19vvaw70l7kr9a].[yr:date_added:ok]</field>
                                </columns>
                              </tuple-descriptor>
                              <tuple>
                                <value>1649</value>
                                <value>2018</value>
                              </tuple>
                            </tuple-reference>
                          </tuple-selection>
                        </selection-collection>
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='This dashboard highlights that TV-MA and TV-14 are the most common ratings, with most shows having only 1 season. Also, average duration varies by rating, with ratings like G and R having longer runtimes compared to TV-Y and TV-Y7.' captured-sheet='Average duration by ratings' id='8' />
                  <story-point caption='This dashboard shows that Rajiv Chilaka and Raúl Campos are among the most frequent directors, and Spike Lee, Scorsese, and Spielberg have worked across 5 genres. Most titles have only 1 season, and Dramas and Comedies dominate in both Movies and TV Shows.' captured-sheet='Most common directors and genres' id='9' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
